# Browser: Orca in-browser first

For localhost / desk UI (verify a page, click through a flow, screenshot),
drive **Orca's embedded browser**. Do not open Playwright MCP,
Chrome DevTools, or system Chrome for that work. Those paths open extra
windows and burn session credits.

Load `orca-cli` then `references/browser.md` before the first tab command.

## Do

- Resolve the CLI: `ORCA_CLI_COMMAND` if set, else `orca`. If that fails
  with a symlink error, use
  `/Applications/Orca.app/Contents/Resources/bin/orca`.
- Open a **new** tab: `orca tab create --url <url> --json`. Stay on that tab.
- Loop: `goto` / `snapshot` / `click --element @eN` / `screenshot`. Re-snapshot
  after navigation or a stale ref.
- Prefer `orca wait --text|--url|--selector|--load` over bare sleeps.

## Browser shares (any page, any task)

Sam may attach a URL, a selected-element dump, HTML, one or more screenshots,
or a mix. The **user query is the task**. The share is evidence of where and
what is on screen. Do not treat an example surface as the thing to build.

**Use:** route; innermost named React component when present (else selector +
visible text); on-screen / aria copy; screenshot(s) as visual truth (several
images are states or viewports); dimensions for density or overflow.

**Ignore unless asked:** full DOM paths, computed-style dumps, truncated SVG,
CDN / asset URLs. Truncated HTML is normal; grep from the component name plus
a stable class or `data-slot`. Do not ask Sam to paste the rest or to change
the share format.

Do not re-dump or re-open the same page before you have used what was shared.
Open a verify tab after you change something, or if the share is not enough
to act. Ask for another crop only when the image hides the thing the query
is about.

## Do not

- Call Playwright or Chrome DevTools MCP (`browser_*` in those namespaces)
  for Edgeways pages.
- Open system Chrome, Chromium, or `open -a "Google Chrome"`.
- Attach to or navigate a tab Sam already has open.
- Use Computer Use for in-app pages (that is for OS windows only).

## Exceptions

- Sam names Playwright / CDP / an external site.
- `browser_host_unavailable` after retry: say so, then use Aside in a
  **new** window (`.cursor/rules/aside-new-window.mdc`). Not Chrome.
